{
  "A document manager in the way code editors arrange files: documents in tabs, tabs in groups, groups split side by side and one under the other. A document's content is any component, a form, a grid or plain text, and it is moved, never made again, when its tab goes to another group. Everything the user does is a method too, asks first and reports after; the whole layout saves to JSON and comes back. Preview and pinned tabs, sizes and copies are on [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs); context menus, lists and keys on [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": "",
  "Documents, groups and splits": "",
  "Make a manager, give it a size, and `open` documents in it. `split` opens a new group beside one; drag the line between two groups (or focus it and use the arrows), double click it to even the sizes, double click a tab to give its group all the room. The buttons at the end of each strip split and maximize.": "",
  "Every behaviour is a prop that takes a value or a function, followed live; a document's own `closable` and `contentLifetime` win over the manager's. Here Alpha cannot be closed and Gamma has unsaved changes.": "",
  "Each thing the user does is also a method (`open`, `close`, `activate`, `split`, `move`, `closeGroup`, `focusGroup`, `maximizeGroup`, `restoreGroups`, `evenSizes`, `resizeGroup`), asks first through a cancelable `on…ing` event and reports through `on…ed`, with `byUser` telling the two apart.": "",
  "Unsaved changes": "",
  "`dirty` follows a function of the form's data: the tab shows a dot in place of its close button. `onClosing` sets `e.promise` to ask; the document closes when the promise says `true`.": "",
  "Saving and restoring the layout": "",
  "`saveLayout()` writes plain JSON: the tree of splits with each child's share, the groups with their documents (`id`, `type`, `title`, `state`, `pinned`, `preview`), the active and recently used tabs, the active and maximized group. `loadLayout(json, factory)` builds it again; the factory makes each document by its `type`.": "",
  "Content lifetime": "",
  "`contentLifetime` decides when a document's content is built and how long it lives. Whatever it is, moving a tab or splitting a group never builds the content again: the same component goes along.": "",
  "Lifetime": "",
  "Built when the document opens; lives, with its state, until it closes.": "",
  "Built the first time it is shown; then kept.": "",
  "Built when shown, disposed when hidden; made again from `content` (or the manager's `factory`) the next time, with the document's `state`. A component given as it is cannot be made again, so it is kept.": "",
  "The keys work while focus is inside the manager; each is a list of chords in `keys`, so any of them can be changed or turned off. A browser tab keeps Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Page Up / Down and often Ctrl+1…9 for itself, so the keys a manager starts with are ones a browser tab lets through, and the desktop key in brackets works too where it can (an installed app takes the desktop keys, `keyPreset`). The recently used list, back and forward, reopening and the other keys are on [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus#keyboard).": "",
  "The next / previous tab of the active group, around the ends (`nextTab`, `previousTab`).": "",
  "Focuses group 1 to 9 (`focusGroup`, written `Ctrl+Alt+{n}`).": "",
  "Splits the active group to the right; the active document goes along when it is not the only one, or a copy of it (`splitRight`).": "",
  "The next / previous, first / last tab; it is activated too unless `activation` is manual (`stripNext`, `stripPrevious`, `stripFirst`, `stripLast`).": "",
  "Activates it.": "",
  "Closes it (`closeFocusedTab`).": "",
  "Make the group before it smaller or larger by `resizeStep`, as small or as large as it can be (`resizeSmaller`, `resizeLarger`, `resizeMin`, `resizeMax`).": "",
  "From the strip (one stop: the active tab) to the group buttons, the content, the splitter, the next group.": "",
  "Each group is a `group` named “Group 1”, “Group 2”…; with `label` the manager is a `region`.": "",
  "A `tablist` per group (“Documents in group 1”) of `tab`s, each controlling its `tabpanel`; a roving `tabindex` keeps one Tab stop per strip. A tab says “unsaved changes” while its document is dirty; `aria-keyshortcuts` names the key that closes it.": "",
  "`separator`s with `aria-orientation`, `aria-valuenow` (the share of the group before it, 0 to 100) and `aria-controls`.": "",
  "A polite live region says what was opened, closed, moved, split, maximized or restored (`announce`).": "",
  "A group remembers what had focus in it; closing the focused tab moves focus to the tab that takes its place.": "",
  "Every text comes from `uiLocale.strings` (`tabDocs…`: the group and strip names, “No open documents”, “unsaved changes”, the buttons, the announcements), in English and Turkish; `texts` changes some for one manager.": "",
  "The root; `data-maximized` while a group is maximized, `data-resizing` while a splitter is dragged; `data-tab-size`, `data-pinned-size`, `data-pinned-row`, `data-wrap`, `data-scroll-buttons` from the props.": "",
  "A split; `data-orientation`.": "",
  "A splitter (`role=\"separator\"`).": "",
  "A group; `data-active`, `data-empty`, `data-maximized`, `data-locked`.": "",
  "The strip row; the tab list with its scroll buttons; the `tablist`, its pinned row and the row of the others; the kit Toolbar with the group buttons.": "",
  "A tab; `aria-selected`, `data-dirty`, `data-close` (`always`, `active`), `data-pinned`, `data-preview`, `data-tone`, `data-icon`.": "",
  "The parts of a tab; a badge that is a dot has `data-dot`.": "",
  "The \"…\" and recently used lists.": "",
  "The content area, a document's `tabpanel`, the empty group's text.": "",
  "Units: behind the groups, a group, its strip and the line under it, the pinned tabs' row, a panel, an empty group's text.": "",
  "Units: a tab (`hover`, `selected`, `before-selected`, `focus`, `dragging`, `title` …; its end side is the line between tabs), the bar on it (`selected`, `active` in the active group), its parts in their tones.": "",
  "Units: the scroll buttons, the thin scrollbar, the count on \"…\", a splitter and its line (`across`, `active`).": "",
  "Sizes the layout counts with (a shrinking tab keeps its icon, its close button and a few letters).": "",
  "Where the bar on a tab stands.": "",
  "The ring's room at a small toolbar's ends; the sizes for a finger.": "",
  "Names the manager: it becomes a `region` landmark. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "Where tabs show a close button: every tab, the active one and the one under the pointer, none. A document with `closable: false` shows none.": "",
  "When content is built and how long it lives (see below). A document's own value wins.": "",
  "A group left without documents closes; the last group never does.": "",
  "Where `open` puts a tab when no `index` is given.": "",
  "Which tab becomes active when the active one closes: the one used last, or a neighbour.": "",
  "`auto`: the arrow keys in a strip activate the tab they reach. `manual`: Enter or Space does.": "",
  "The smallest size of a group, in pixels; a splitter stops there.": "",
  "How far a splitter key moves a splitter, in pixels.": "",
  "The split, maximize and \"…\" buttons at the end of each strip.": "",
  "A double click on a tab maximizes its group, or restores the groups (a preview tab is kept open instead).": "",
  "The keys a manager starts with: keys a browser tab lets through, or a desktop editor's; `auto` takes the desktop keys in an installed app.": "",
  "Changes some keys; the others keep the preset's. An empty list turns a key off.": "",
  "Makes the content of a document that brings none, usually by its `type`.": "",
  "Texts for this manager only, over `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "Opened, closed, moved, split, maximized: said politely to screen readers.": "",
  "Stays the same for the document's life; made up when left out. `findDocument(id)` finds it.": "",
  "The key a layout is restored by: the `loadLayout` factory and the manager's `factory` read it.": "",
  "The tab's text; the description follows it, quieter, and tells two documents of the same title apart.": "",
  "An icon before the title; a short text or count after it.": "",
  "Shown when the pointer rests on the tab or the tab has focus. Default: the title and the description.": "",
  "Unsaved changes: a dot takes the close button's place (the button comes back under the pointer), and screen readers hear “unsaved changes”.": "",
  "Default `true`. `false`: no close button, and the user cannot close it (code still can).": "",
  "A pinned tab stays at the start; a preview tab gives its place to the next preview. Saved with the layout. See [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs).": "",
  "A count or a dot, a colour, toolbar buttons while active, a copy's content. See [Tabs](/tabdocs/tabs) and [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": "",
  "This document's own lifetime; `undefined` follows the manager.": "",
  "The content: a component, or a function that makes it (and makes it again after `dispose`).": "",
  "The app's own data for the document, saved with the layout.": "",
  "Where it is open, and the content made for it.": "",
  "The same as the manager's methods.": "",
  "The groups in layout order: left to right, top to bottom.": "",
  "Every open document, group by group.": "",
  "The group that has focus or had it last, and its active document.": "",
  "The maximized group, `null` when none is.": "",
  "The documents used last, the ones `reopenClosed` can open, and the history. See [Menus and keys](/tabdocs/menus).": "",
  "static": "",
  "The two key presets.": "",
  "In strip order; the active one; the one used last first.": "",
  "Its place in `groups`, from 0, and its state.": "",
  "A locked group takes no document opened without naming the group. `lock()` and `unlock()` ask first and announce it.": "",
  "The group's preview tab's document, if it has one.": "",
  "The manager's methods for this group.": "",
  "Opens a `TabDocument` (or one made from options) in a group, the active one by default; a document already open is activated. `null` when `onOpening` cancels.": "",
  "Closes as the close button does; `false` when `onClosing` keeps it.": "",
  "Closes the documents of a group, or of all of them; `false` when some stay.": "",
  "Makes it its group's active tab and its group the active group; `focus` moves focus into the content.": "",
  "The next or previous tab, around the ends (Ctrl + Page Down / Up).": "",
  "To another place in its group, or to another group. The content goes along as it is.": "",
  "A new group on the `'left'`, `'right'`, `'up'` or `'down'` side; `doc` moves into it. `group` `null`: along that edge of the whole layout.": "",
  "Closes its documents, then the group. The last group stays, empty.": "",
  "Makes it active and focuses what had focus in it last.": "",
  "One group takes all the room; the others wait, out of sight, as they were.": "",
  "Every group of every split the same size.": "",
  "A group's size along its split: pixels or a share (`'30%'`); the neighbour after it gives or takes the room.": "",
  "The layout as plain JSON (see below).": "",
  "Puts a saved layout in place of the current one, whose documents close without asking. `factory(saved)` returns the document, its options or its content.": "",
  "`{ document, group, index, active, byUser }`; `opening` is cancelable and may change `group` and `index`.": "",
  "`{ document, group, index, byUser }`; `closing` is cancelable, or sets `e.promise` (`Promise<boolean>`) to ask first.": "",
  "`{ document, previous, group, byUser }`; `activating` (a tab is selected) is cancelable; `activated` also runs when another group becomes active.": "",
  "`{ document, from, fromIndex, to, toIndex, byUser }`; `moving` is cancelable.": "",
  "`{ group, direction, document, byUser }` (and `newGroup` after); `splitting` is cancelable. `group` is `null` when the new group goes along an edge of the whole layout.": "",
  "`{ change, group, byUser }`, `change` one of `'split'`, `'closeGroup'`, `'resize'`, `'evenSizes'`, `'maximize'`, `'restore'`, `'move'` (a whole group moved or merged), `'load'`; `changing` is cancelable (a split asks through `onSplitting`).": ""
